WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.102
-We're just over a month away

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.503
from the end
of the Trump administration,

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.939
and there are two things we know
for certain about this president

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.008
and his enablers
that we should never forget.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:12.945
They tried to end democracy and
they tried to get people sick.

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.381
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:19.419 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:22.421
There's a sense among some
Democrats, including apparently

00:00:22.421 --> 00:00:24.057
President-elect
Joe Biden himself,

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.226
that Republicans
will just calm down

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.626
and become reasonable again

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:29.829
after Donald Trump
is off the political stage,

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.464
which is unlikely
for two reasons.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:34.867
One, Trump will never
willingly leave the stage.

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.735
If he ever performed
at the Apollo,

00:00:36.735 --> 00:00:39.105
he'd be the first contestant
to get into a fistfight

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.573
with the Sandman.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.008
Trump's like someone who draws
out the "Happy Birthday" song

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:46.812
with lots of trills and "ayyyys"
when the rest of the office

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:49.515
wants to get back to work
and the Carvel cake is like,

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:50.950
"I'm melting over here."

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.586
It's basically a guarantee
that for the next four years,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.888
he's going to be tweeting,
holding rallies,

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.323
and calling into Fox News

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.625
for those three-hour-long
therapy sessions

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.095
where the "Fox &amp; Friends"
look like tourists

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.429
trapped on a subway car

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:06.398
with the guy feeding
the dead mouse to his pet Cobra.

00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:08.334
I mean, Brian Kilmeade
already looks like

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.770
he's the only claymation
anchor at Fox News.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.673
But when he doesn't blink
for an hour straight,

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:16.009
you'd think he was a
lesser-known Gumby character.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.143
He's Dumby.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.779
And the second reason --
that Republicans

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.113
weren't reasonable before Trump.

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:23.783
So there's no reasonable
to go back to.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.986
A decade ago, they were famously
showing up to town halls

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.522
demanding to see Barack Obama's
birth certificate

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.223
and walking around D.C.

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.560
wearing long coats
and tricorn hats

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.729
like they waited too long to go
to Party City before Halloween.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.165
"I'm a zombie, but from colonial
times.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.000
Look, it's all they had left,
man."

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.437
And yet Biden seems intent on
trying to appeal to Republicans

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.473
in an attempt to return
to a bipartisan normalcy

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:48.641
that is impossible.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.510
And even if it was possible,

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.144
it wasn't working
for most people.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:55.047
Biden is reportedly considering
picking a Republican

00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:56.349
to be Commerce Secretary.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:58.084
And on Monday,
he told supporters

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.752
that Republicans
would come around

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.887
and return to normal
once Trump is gone.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:05.191
-I predict to you,
and I may eat these words,

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.861
but I predict to you,
as Donald Trump's shadow

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:12.131
fades away, you're going to see
an awful lot change.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:15.768
-And I may eat these words,
but, dude...

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.870
Don't get me wrong --
after the last four years,

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.073
it'll be nice to have
a president who's optimistic.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.241
But sometimes optimism
can backfire.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:24.409
Biden is like a football coach
in a sports movie

00:02:24.409 --> 00:02:25.578
who says to a player,

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.313
"You may be the smallest kid
on this team,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.647
but you got the biggest heart.

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:30.449
Now you go show him
what you can do!"

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:33.386
Then a week later, he's sitting
next to the hospital bed saying,

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.755
"Doc told me you broke
the leg in 50 places!

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.623
I didn't even know
that was possible!"

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.058
When it comes
to the Republican Party,

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.661
Donald Trump's shadow is
not just going to fade away,

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.195
at least not for a long time.

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:45.131
It probably won't even
leave the White House.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.500
I wouldn't be surprised
if even after he leaves,

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.536
it's still there
wandering around alone,

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.804
where he used to
scream-answer questions

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.073
over the sound
of a helicopter engine.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.376
If anything, they should
preserve his shadow.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.278
His profile is so weird,
scientists should study it.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:02.348
"Based on this shadow, what do
you think happened next?"

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.515
"He fell over forward?"

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:04.917
"No, he didn't.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:08.855
It always looked like he was
about to, but he never did."

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:11.724
There are certainly no signs yet
that Republicans will suddenly

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.692
stop caring what Trump
thinks of them.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.194
Even after he lost the election

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.697
and they were free of the need
to do his bidding,

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.232
they still tried to overthrow
democracy just to please him.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:23.369
They know he's tapped into the
heart of the Republican base,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.471
and they live in fear
of a primary challenge

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.973
or a nasty tweet from him.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:30.709
-I think we know from what we've
seen with Republicans so far,

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:33.513
they're going to get on board
with this president.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:38.450
There is no evidence to suggest
that there are Republicans

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.853
who want to cross
this president,

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.856
even though he has lost
this election.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:47.693
They know he wants to remain
in power out of office,

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:49.895
and they're going to do
everything they can

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.631
to show this president loyalty.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:54.200
They're going to do that
because they know if they don't,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.735
this president
will tweet something.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:59.271
Maybe he will back a primary
challenger against them.

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.674
So, no, I don't think there's
going to be any division.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.243
The choice that Republicans
have had to make

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:07.513
is either be fully on board
with Donald Trump

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.515
or essentially leave the party.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.818
-Yeah, it's like when you were
in high school at a party

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:13.386
in a friend's basement
late at night

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.987
and everyone started
doing whippets.

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:18.257
You can't just stand in a corner
and hope no one notices you.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:20.727
you either man up and start
killing off brain cells

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.561
or go party with the chess club.

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:24.630
And again,
that joke is about chess

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.599
when I was in high school
and not now

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.401
when it's the hottest sport
in the goddamn world!

00:04:29.401 --> 00:04:31.804
So turned on by chess,
I've started to refer to it

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:34.273
as pawnography.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:35.507
Hit me with the crickets, Alex.

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:36.843
[ Crickets chirping ]

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.377
There it is.

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.213
Think about how servile
and cowardly you have to be

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.613
to live in fear of a nasty tweet

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:44.183
from the world's pettiest,
most irritating man.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:47.119
I mean, he's tweeted
about me like 20 times,

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.922
including when he called me
"bland, weak, awkward,

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.323
and insecure," and said,

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:53.459
"His show is a cure for
insomnia," which is ridiculous.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.626
You can't call it a cure yet

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:56.262
because we're still
in clinical trials.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.197
Although early results
do suggest that our show

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.332
is 95% effective
at inducing sleep,

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.401
which is on par with Lunesta.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:05.037
I'm coming for you, glow moth!

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:07.240
Also, you know why I think
Biden is wrong about this?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.075
Because he was wrong
when he said basically

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.542
the exact same thing
eight years ago

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:12.078
before the 2012 election.

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:13.379
-I've said this to you before.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.013
What we need
is a Republican Party.

00:05:15.013 --> 00:05:17.516
We need leaders
that can control their party.

00:05:17.516 --> 00:05:19.418
And I think you're going
to see the fever break.

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:22.221
-Not only did the fever
not break, it's spread.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.756
Now we have to get
our temperatures checked

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.291
before we walk into
an Applebee's.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.359
Biden thought the GOP's fever
would break,

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:28.594
and instead they elected a guy

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.730
who gave as many people fevers
as he could.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.132
And even before that,
he just always looked like

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:34.900
he had a fever -- flush, sweaty.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.303
He's basically every side effect
at the end of a drug commercial

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.504
rolled into one person.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.506
The point is,
this is the Republican Party.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:41.941
Trump is not an anomaly.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:44.410
It was an unhinged authoritarian
movement before Trump,

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.711
and it's not going
to change now.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:48.314
I mean, look at what they've
been saying even after

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:51.283
the courts and even the Trump
supporting attorney general

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:53.886
repeatedly made it clear
there was no evidence of fraud,

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.754
let alone widespread fraud

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:57.590
that would have changed
the outcome of the election.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.192
-A large percentage
of the American public

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:02.594
does not believe the November
election results are legitimate.

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:05.431
-You think the election
was stolen, you tweeted out?

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.767
-Absolutely. I think there's
a great deal of fraud.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.803
-As we await today's
Electoral College decision,

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.505
an intel source telling me
that President Trump did,

00:06:13.505 --> 00:06:15.141
in fact, win the election.

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:17.843
He says that it is up
to the Supreme Court

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.545
to hear suits from other cases

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:22.181
across the country
to stop the clock.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.482
-There are two
possibilities here.

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.051
One, an intel source with proof

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.786
of the election fraud chose
not to make that proof public,

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:29.822
but instead called
Maria Bartiromo

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.657
when it was too late
to change the outcome,

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:34.760
or two, one time,
Maria Bartiromo

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.629
yelled at the paper boy
for throwing her copy

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.263
of "The Bat[bleep] Times"
in her hedges,

00:06:38.263 --> 00:06:41.133
and now he prank calls her
with hot tips.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.202
"And you're saying Donald Trump
won the election?"

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:47.006
"Yeah, by, like, a lot."

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:49.775
Also, notice how Republicans
do this little rhetorical trick

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:52.144
where they claim that because
their voters

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:53.579
think the election was rigged,

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.848
that means we have to
restore faith in our elections.

00:06:56.848 --> 00:06:59.919
-It is a serious problem
when you don't have confidence,

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:02.020
when such a high number
of Americans

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.390
don't have confidence in
the legitimacy of the election.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:08.928
-Yesterday, I was talking with
some of the constituents

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.696
back at home,
group of about 30 people.

00:07:11.696 --> 00:07:15.033
Every single one of them,

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:17.503
every one of them told me

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.605
that they felt
they had been disenfranchized,

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.307
that their votes didn't matter,

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:23.509
that the election
had been rigged.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:26.012
These are normal,
reasonable people.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:27.646
These are not crazy people.

00:07:27.646 --> 00:07:29.414
-If they do think the election
is rigged,

00:07:29.414 --> 00:07:32.718
it's only because you guys
keep telling them it's rigged.

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:34.953
You're the ones
causing this problem.

00:07:34.953 --> 00:07:37.456
You can't then turn around
and say you want to solve it.

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:39.425
These guys are like bank robbers
stuffing cash

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.792
in a duffel bag saying,
"By the way,

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:42.794
you should really get some
security cameras in here."

00:07:42.794 --> 00:07:44.463
The Republican Party
has spent the last month

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.331
actively trying to dismantle
our democracy.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:48.667
There's no reason to believe
they'll suddenly change

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:51.002
and every reason to believe
this is who they really are.

00:07:51.002 --> 00:07:54.072
I mean, the president himself
is apparently threatening

00:07:54.072 --> 00:07:56.208
in private
not to leave the White House.

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:58.911
-Sources tell CNN that
the president has pulled a 180.

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.979
He used to privately
accept the reality

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:02.448
that he lost the election.

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.582
But now, no.

00:08:03.582 --> 00:08:05.517
He's now starting
to believe his own lies,

00:08:05.517 --> 00:08:06.852
that the election was stolen.

00:08:06.852 --> 00:08:09.655
So much so that Trump
has told some advisers

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.256
that he may not leave
the White House

00:08:11.256 --> 00:08:15.294
on Inauguration Day --
literally saying such a thing,

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:17.029
putting words to the sentiment.

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:18.965
And one adviser telling CNN,

00:08:18.965 --> 00:08:20.799
"He's throwing an effing
temper tantrum.

00:08:20.799 --> 00:08:22.935
He's going to leave.
He's just lashing out."

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:24.236
-He's like a kid who refuses

00:08:24.236 --> 00:08:26.072
to leave the ball pit
at Chuck E. Cheese.

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.239
"Atticus!

00:08:27.239 --> 00:08:29.709
Atticus, where are you?!
Atticus?!"

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:31.677
"Sir, adults aren't allowed
in the ball pit."

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.111
"I'm looking for my son.

00:08:33.111 --> 00:08:35.147
Told him we have to leave,
but he refuses to accept

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.216
the results of the ball pit!
Atticus?!"

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:38.917
Obviously,
Trump won't be allowed

00:08:38.917 --> 00:08:40.586
to stay in the White House,
but the fact that he's even

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:42.320
talking about it is insane.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:43.756
I mean, what does he think
is going to happen?

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:45.758
Biden's going to move in,
and they're going to have to

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:48.793
share a bunk bed
like freshman year roommates?

00:08:48.793 --> 00:08:52.231
[ As Trump ] Joe? Joe?

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:54.766
Joe?

00:08:54.766 --> 00:08:57.002
Are you awake, Joe? Joe?

00:08:57.002 --> 00:08:59.138
[ As Biden ]
What is it, Donny?

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:01.206
[ As Trump ] Do you think...

00:09:01.206 --> 00:09:03.209
Rudy is a bad lawyer?

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:06.212
[ Laughter ]

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:07.813
[ Normal voice ] And even after
the Electoral College

00:09:07.813 --> 00:09:10.282
made it official on Monday,
Trump's allies on Fox News

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:12.718
are still acting like
there's some possibility

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:14.219
he could subvert
the will of the voters,

00:09:14.219 --> 00:09:16.188
overturn the election,
and remain in office.

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:18.591
They can barely even bring
themselves to say the words

00:09:18.591 --> 00:09:20.091
"President-elect Joe Biden."

00:09:20.091 --> 00:09:21.527
-Steve Doocy's son Peter,

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:23.695
who has been
on the campaign trail,

00:09:23.695 --> 00:09:26.498
and now he's with
what they're calling

00:09:26.498 --> 00:09:28.267
the President-elect Biden.

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:30.803
-So does it bother you at all
that the son

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:33.873
of the former vice president,
who is,

00:09:33.873 --> 00:09:36.242
according to some,
president-elect...

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:38.877
-Oh, Dumby. What do you mean,
according to some?

00:09:38.877 --> 00:09:41.313
The Electoral College
literally just certified it.

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:43.649
The highest court in the country
has affirmed it twice.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:44.983
Now it's not a matter
of opinion.

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:46.418
Joe Biden
is the president-elect.

00:09:46.418 --> 00:09:47.953
These guys are talking about it

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:50.322
like we're all debating
the best Billy Joel song.

00:09:50.322 --> 00:09:52.525
"According to some, it's 'Scenes
from an Italian Restaurant,'

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:54.593
but I think it's that weird
instrumental song

00:09:54.593 --> 00:09:56.695
that sounds like the music
at a grocery store."

00:09:56.695 --> 00:10:00.365
[ Soft piano music plays ]

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:03.802
All jokes aside, the best
Billy Joel song is "Vienna."

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:06.438
Oh, sure, you have your "Summer,
Highland Falls" dead-enders

00:10:06.438 --> 00:10:07.740
and your "She's Got a Way"
heads,

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.844
but it's "Vienna," hands down,
debate over.

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:13.612
Again, there's no reason
to simply act like

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:15.114
the last four years didn't
happen

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:17.483
and the people that enabled
this monstrous administration

00:10:17.483 --> 00:10:20.686
will suddenly become reasonable
participants in democracy again.

00:10:20.686 --> 00:10:23.521
In fact, yesterday we found
from blockbuster new reporting

00:10:23.521 --> 00:10:24.756
that a Trump appointee

00:10:24.756 --> 00:10:26.391
at the Department of Health
and Human Services

00:10:26.391 --> 00:10:28.126
actively advised the government

00:10:28.126 --> 00:10:30.363
to let as many people
get coronavirus as possible.

00:10:30.363 --> 00:10:33.165
While we all basically knew that
already

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:34.800
from, you know,
our eyes and ears,

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.369
seeing it written down
in an email was still shocking.

00:10:37.369 --> 00:10:39.671
-New emails reported
by Politico today

00:10:39.671 --> 00:10:42.241
show a Trump administration
official back in July

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:45.410
pushing the widely discredited
theory of herd immunity,

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.914
the idea of purposefully
infecting people,

00:10:48.914 --> 00:10:50.849
wrote the then science adviser,

00:10:50.849 --> 00:10:53.819
"Infants, kids, teens,
young people, young adults,

00:10:53.819 --> 00:10:55.854
middle-aged with no conditions,
et cetera,

00:10:55.854 --> 00:10:59.425
have zero to little risk,
so we use them to develop herd.

00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:04.062
We want them infected
and recovered with antibodies."

00:11:04.062 --> 00:11:05.765
We want them infected.

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:08.901
Experts say that would be
a disastrous course,

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:12.237
though it might explain
the refusal of the White House

00:11:12.237 --> 00:11:14.939
to do more to stop the spread.

00:11:14.939 --> 00:11:16.775
-"We want them infected."

00:11:16.775 --> 00:11:19.545
That is some real super villain
[bleep] right there.

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:21.546
I mean, Bane might say that,

00:11:21.546 --> 00:11:23.882
but even he wouldn't
put it down in an email.

00:11:23.882 --> 00:11:25.550
[ As Bane ]
Batman, don't you see?

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:27.186
We want them infected!

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:30.489
CCing Alfred to make sure
you get eyes on this.

00:11:30.489 --> 00:11:34.293
[ Normal voice ] Shoemaker,
my Bane's getting better.

00:11:34.293 --> 00:11:35.794
No thanks to you.

00:11:35.794 --> 00:11:36.995
[ Laughter ]

00:11:36.995 --> 00:11:38.096
Every day I try to run

00:11:38.096 --> 00:11:39.865
my Bane lines with Shoemaker.

00:11:39.865 --> 00:11:40.899
"Oh, I'm too busy."

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:42.534
"With what?" I ask.

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:45.470
"Every part of this show
that's not you reading jokes

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:49.041
off cue cards," he says,
hurting my feelings.

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.408
How dare you!

00:11:50.408 --> 00:11:52.044
On our Christmas show, no less!

00:11:52.044 --> 00:11:56.982
[ Laughter ]

00:11:56.982 --> 00:11:59.251
Just think about how monstrous
and sociopathic that is.

00:11:59.251 --> 00:12:00.686
They wanted people to get sick.

00:12:00.686 --> 00:12:03.488
I know in the Trump era, every
news story last five minutes

00:12:03.488 --> 00:12:05.257
and our brains have
all been turned to mush

00:12:05.257 --> 00:12:06.825
by the constant
crush of insanity.

00:12:06.825 --> 00:12:09.161
But this story
should never be forgotten.

00:12:09.161 --> 00:12:11.630
Anyone who enabled this should
be held accountable for it.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.598
You can't just let
something like this go.

00:12:13.598 --> 00:12:15.333
If you go through
your spouse's things

00:12:15.333 --> 00:12:17.870
and find a bunch of love letters
to an ex saying,

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.137
"I want my husband to die,"

00:12:19.137 --> 00:12:21.172
you don't just toss it
in the trash and say,

00:12:21.172 --> 00:12:23.508
"Oh, well,
water under the bridge."

00:12:23.508 --> 00:12:25.210
The Trump administration
may be coming to an end,

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:27.846
but there's no reason to think
this era in our politics

00:12:27.846 --> 00:12:29.247
will end any time soon.

00:12:29.247 --> 00:12:32.017
Trump has exposed a deep rot
in our political system

00:12:32.017 --> 00:12:33.451
and within the Republican Party

00:12:33.451 --> 00:12:35.687
that isn't going to just
magically disappear.

00:12:35.687 --> 00:12:37.590
And we can't just forget
what happened here.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.124
They tried to destroy
our democracy

00:12:39.124 --> 00:12:41.226
and they stood by
as Americans died.

00:12:41.226 --> 00:12:43.629
Say what you will about
the Republican establishment,

00:12:43.629 --> 00:12:45.731
but at the very least,
it's clear they're either

00:12:45.731 --> 00:12:48.634
dishonest people,
corrupt people, or...

00:12:48.634 --> 00:12:49.901
-Crazy people.

00:12:49.901 --> 00:12:51.637
-This has been "A Closer Look."

